cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "GPU MODE linear-algebra kernel audit, 2026: results record"
message: >-
  If you use this record, cite it as below. When you use the GPU MODE material, also link
  the GPU MODE dataset and cite KernelBot, as the dataset card requests (see references).
  The audit's own results are CC BY 4.0, the code (scripts/, replay/, qr/randsvd.py) is
  MIT, and the material from GPU MODE stays under its licenses (see the README).
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Melnichenko
    given-names: Maksim
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0007-7749-188X"
    affiliation: "International Computer Science Institute and University of California, Berkeley"
version: 1.0.1
date-released: 2026-11-10
license: CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/VSCL-x-VERITAS/gpumode-kernel-audit-2026"
abstract: >-
  Results of an independent audit of the five top-ranked entries on each of the four
  leaderboards of the 2026 GPU MODE competitions for fast GPU linear-algebra kernels:
  batched QR factorization (two rounds), batched Cholesky factorization, and batched
  symmetric eigendecomposition. Each entry was run unmodified through the organizers' own
  checker on further legal inputs, on NVIDIA B200 GPUs. All twenty entries passed the
  scored cases of their own round, and eighteen failed the same checker on other legal
  inputs on which the vendor routine passed. The record holds the verdicts, a description
  of every recorded evaluation, the hashes of the entries, checkers and environments, and a script that
  replays a QR evaluation from the entry file (the round-2 entry files are public).
keywords:
  - numerical linear algebra
  - GPU kernels
  - QR factorization
  - Cholesky factorization
  - symmetric eigendecomposition
  - accuracy testing
  - GPU MODE
